# An allowlist: everything is out of the build context, and only what the image
# is built from comes back in. From the source trees that is Python source and
# the packages' py.typed, so a key or credential lying beside the code never
# reaches the wheels. Upstream's flash_head tree comes whole, because the
# provider's wheel packs it with its configuration files.
*
!LICENSE
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/**/*.py
!packages/client/pyproject.toml
!packages/client/src/**/*.py
!packages/client/src/**/py.typed
!providers/fake/pyproject.toml
!providers/provider-contract/pyproject.toml
!providers/provider-contract/src/**/*.py
!providers/provider-contract/src/**/py.typed
!providers/flashhead-lite/LICENSE
!providers/flashhead-lite/pyproject.toml
!providers/flashhead-lite/uv.lock
!providers/flashhead-lite/src/**/*.py
!providers/flashhead-lite/src/**/py.typed
!providers/flashhead-lite/soulx-flashhead/LICENSE
!providers/flashhead-lite/soulx-flashhead/flash_head/**

# Nested repositories, environments and tool caches can hold Python files too.
**/.git/**
**/.venv/**
**/__pycache__/**
**/.*_cache/**
**/node_modules/**
